.TH DM 1 "2026-11-06" "dm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dm \- durable terminal multiplexer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dm
[\fIcommand\fP] [\fIoptions\fP]
.br
.B dm
[\fB\-s\fP \fIname\fP]
.SH COMMANDS
A command is the first word after dm. With no command, dm attaches to a session, creating it if needed.
.TP
\fBdm [-s name]\fP
attach to a session, creating it if needed
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm attach [-s name]\fP
attach to a session, creating it if needed
.br
Aliases: a.
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm new [-s name]\fP
start a session without attaching
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm ls\fP
list sessions and whether they are live
.br
Aliases: list-sessions.
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--json\fP print JSON
.TP
\fBdm kill [-s name]\fP
stop a session's server (panes survive)
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm purge [--dry-run]\fP
remove dead sessions whose panes are gone
.br
\fB--dry-run\fP print what would be removed
.TP
\fBdm exec '<json>' [-s name]\fP
send an action as JSON
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--action-json\fP action JSON
.br
Example: \fBdm exec '{"action":"split","target":"p1","dir":"right"}'\fP
.TP
\fBdm write-to <pane> --msg T\fP
type text into a pane (--enter to accept)
.br
Aliases: write.
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--msg\fP message text
.br
\fB--enter\fP press enter after the message
.br
Example: \fBdm write-to p1 --msg 'ls -la' --enter\fP
.TP
\fBdm read <pane> [--lines N]\fP
print a pane's screen
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--lines N\fP number of screen lines
.br
\fB--scrollback N\fP history rows above the screen
.br
\fBdm read <pane> --scrollback N\fP print N rows above the screen
.TP
\fBdm split <pane> --dir D\fP
split a pane: left right up down
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--dir D\fP split direction: left right up down
.br
\fB--json\fP print JSON
.TP
\fBdm focus <pane>\fP
focus a pane
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm rename-workspace <ws> <name>\fP
rename a workspace
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm next-pane\fP
focus the next pane
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm prev-pane\fP
focus the previous pane
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm new-window\fP
open a new window
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm next-window\fP
focus the next window
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm prev-window\fP
focus the previous window
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm status [pane]\fP
show OSC 7501 agent status
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm list\fP
print the pane tree as JSON
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--json\fP print JSON
.TP
\fBdm dash [-s name]\fP
print the palette rows
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm peek <id> [--lines N]\fP
print the screen a palette row lands on
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--lines N\fP number of screen lines
.TP
\fBdm msg post --state S [--key K] [--msg T]\fP
post one entry to the box
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--state S\fP box state: note working blocked done error
.br
\fB--key K\fP box key
.br
\fB--msg\fP message text
.br
Example: \fBdm msg post --key build --state done --msg 'all green'\fP
.TP
\fBdm msg list [--key K | --prefix P] [--after SEQ] [--limit N] [--json]\fP
print the box newest first
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--key K\fP box key
.br
\fB--prefix P\fP box key prefix
.br
\fB--after SEQ\fP box seq cursor: entries after this one
.br
\fB--limit N\fP list rows, 0 for the whole box
.br
\fB--json\fP print JSON
.TP
\fBdm msg wait [--key K | --prefix P] [--state S] [--after SEQ] [--timeout 5m]\fP
block until an entry matches
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--key K\fP box key
.br
\fB--prefix P\fP box key prefix
.br
\fB--state S\fP box state: note working blocked done error
.br
\fB--after SEQ\fP box seq cursor: entries after this one
.br
\fB--timeout D\fP wait timeout
.br
Example: \fBdm msg wait --key build --state done --timeout 10m\fP
.TP
\fBdm msg sub [--key K | --prefix P] [--state S] [--after SEQ] [--json]\fP
stream entries as they arrive
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--key K\fP box key
.br
\fB--prefix P\fP box key prefix
.br
\fB--state S\fP box state: note working blocked done error
.br
\fB--after SEQ\fP box seq cursor: entries after this one
.br
\fB--json\fP print JSON
.br
Example: \fBdm msg sub --prefix build --json\fP
.TP
\fBdm msg clear [--key K]\fP
clear one key, or the whole box
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--key K\fP box key
.TP
\fBdm msg watchers [--json]\fP
print the live watches
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.br
\fB--json\fP print JSON
.TP
\fBdm msg schema\fP
print the box schema the server serves
.br
\fB--s name\fP session name
.TP
\fBdm man [-o path]\fP
print the man page, or write it to a file
.br
\fB--o path\fP write the page to this path
.SH ACTIONS
dm exec takes one JSON object. The fields are:
.TP
\fBaction\fP
the action name, required
.TP
\fBtarget\fP
the pane, window or workspace id the action acts on
.TP
\fBdir\fP
split or focus direction: left, right, up or down
.TP
\fBother\fP
resize-split: the pane on the other side of the split
.TP
\fBmsg\fP
text to type into a pane
.TP
\fBenter\fP
press enter after msg
.TP
\fBname\fP
a new name for a window, workspace or pane
.TP
\fBwindow\fP
new-workspace: the window name
.TP
\fBindex\fP
select-window: the window number; set-rail: the rail width
.TP
\fBid\fP
request id, echoed in the reply
.TP
\fBcwd\fP
working directory for a new pane, window or workspace
.TP
\fBratio\fP
split ratio, 0 to 1
.TP
\fBnofocus\fP
do not move focus to the new pane
.TP
\fBcols\fP
terminal columns
.TP
\fBrows\fP
terminal rows
.TP
\fBkeys\fP
raw bytes to write to a pane
.TP
\fBdata\fP
raw bytes
.TP
\fBcount\fP
history rows above the screen
.TP
\fBres\fP
the verb payload for the msg-* actions
.PP
The action field names one of: ping, list, read, history, replay, status, write-to, exec, keys, split, zoom-pane, set-rail, resize-split, focus, focus-dir, next-pane, prev-pane, close-pane, close-window, new-window, next-window, prev-window, select-window, new-workspace, next-workspace, prev-workspace, list-workspaces, list-panes, pane, toggle-fold, set-pane-name, focus-window, focus-workspace, close-workspace, rename-window, rename-workspace, msg-post, msg-list, msg-clear, msg-wait, msg-sub, msg-watchers, msg-schema.
.SH KEYS
The default keymap. A key label is the key pressed after the prefix key.
.TP
\fB|\fP
split right
.TP
\fB-\fP
split down
.TP
\fB< / ^\fP
split left / up
.TP
\fB[\fP
scrollback
.TP
\fBh j k l\fP
focus pane
.TP
\fBn / p\fP
next/prev pane
.TP
\fBx\fP
close pane
.TP
\fBX\fP
close window
.TP
\fBz\fP
zoom pane
.TP
\fBc\fP
new window
.TP
\fBw / W\fP
next/prev win
.TP
\fB0-9\fP
select window
.TP
\fBt\fP
new workspace
.TP
\fB)\fP
next workspace
.TP
\fBs\fP
switch session
.TP
\fBr\fP
rename workspace
.TP
\fBm\fP
message box
.TP
\fBb\fP
cycle rail: full, thin, hidden
.TP
\fBd / q\fP
detach
.TP
\fBctrl+b\fP
send prefix
.TP
\fBctrl+r\fP
reload config
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$DM_STATE/sessions/<name>/state.json\fP
.TP
\fB$DM_STATE/sessions/<name>/server.sock\fP
.TP
\fB$DM_STATE/sessions/<name>/panes/<id>.sock\fP
.TP
\fB$DM_STATE/sessions/<name>/panes/<id>.log\fP
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dm/config.kdl\fP
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBDM_STATE\fP
state directory; overrides XDG_STATE_HOME
.TP
\fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fP
state directory base; dm uses $XDG_STATE_HOME/dm
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fP
config directory base; dm reads $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dm/config.kdl
.TP
\fBDM_SESSION\fP
the session a pane belongs to; dm refuses to attach that session from inside it
.TP
\fBDM_PANE\fP
the pane id a pane's shell runs in
.TP
\fBDM_NERD\fP
1 forces Nerd font glyphs, 0 forces the Unicode fallback
.TP
\fBDM_NOTIFY\fP
0 turns desktop notifications off
.TP
\fBCOLUMNS\fP
terminal width when the client cannot ask the terminal
.TP
\fBSHELL\fP
the shell a new pane runs
.TP
\fBTMUX\fP
set inside tmux; dm uses it to pick its terminal behaviour
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1)
